# Copy this file to .env for local development (the dev server and BFF read .env; the browser build reads .env.local for VITE_ vars).
#
# Server-side (the BFF under api/ — `vercel dev` reads .env.local too):
#   ZOHO_CLIENT_ID / ZOHO_CLIENT_SECRET / ZOHO_REFRESH_TOKEN / ZOHO_BASE_ID
#   ZOHO_DC (default tables.zoho.in), ALLOW_DEV_SESSION=1 for the dev fallback session
#   KINDE_DOMAIN once the tenant exists; KINDE_AUDIENCE only if you adopt a Kinde
#   API audience (the SPA's own access token needs none — leave it unset)
# These are secrets — they stay server-side and must never gain a VITE_ prefix.
#
# Browser-side (Kinde SPA credentials, all optional — absent means the dev session):
# VITE_KINDE_DOMAIN=
# VITE_KINDE_CLIENT_ID=
# VITE_KINDE_REDIRECT_URI=          # http://localhost:3000 locally (scripts/dev-server.mjs)
# VITE_KINDE_LOGOUT_URI=
#
# Kinde dashboard, once: Settings > Applications > [app] > Details > Tokens >
# Token customization > Access token > Customize — tick `roles` and `email`.
# Without it the access token carries neither claim: every caller reads as an
# Operator and the audit trail falls back to the Kinde user id.
